  "name": "kimchi-playground",
  "description": "A sophisticated suite of zero-knowledge proof system components centered on the Kimchi PLONKish arithmetization and the Pickles inductive recursion framework. It provides high-performance implementations of cryptographic primitives including the Pasta elliptic curve cycle, Poseidon transcript hashing, and optimized polynomial commitment schemes. The repository also features the Snarky circuit-writing DSL and a ZK-VM implementation targeting MIPS-based fault proofs for the Optimism rollup stack.",
